@startuml
title Actlane MCP Broker — Safe Dynamic Capability Flow

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F8F8F8
  BorderColor #333333
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam diamond {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
  BorderColor #333333
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EEF7FF
  BorderColor #4A90E2
}

|AI Coder Agent|

start

:User task received;
note right
Example:
"Поправь sandbox terraform"
"Обнови зависимость"
"Почини деплой"
end note

:Call stable MCP tool:
actlane_classify;

|Actlane MCP Broker|

:Collect facts;
note right
Inputs:
- user task
- repo tree
- changed files
- git diff
- branch
- existing configs
- .actlane/policy.yaml
end note

:Detect primary work type;

note right
Primary work types:
- docs_change
- test_change
- code_change
- dependency_change
- config_change
- ci_change
- infra_change
- deployment_change
- data_migration_change
- unknown_or_mixed
end note

:Detect risk flags;

note right
Risk flags:
- secrets_sensitive
- production_sensitive
- destructive_operation
- security_sensitive
- public_api_sensitive
end note

if (Intent clear?) then (yes)
  :Build Intent Envelope;
else (no)
  :Set work_type = unknown_or_mixed;
  :Reduce permissions;
endif

:Match technology hints;

note right
Technology hints are not core intents.
They only select profiles.

Examples:
- terraform
- nodejs/npm
- python/fastapi
- kubernetes
- docker
- ios
end note

:Select candidate profiles;

note right
Examples:
- terraform_readonly
- nodejs_dependency
- python_web
- generic_docs
- ci_pipeline
- k8s_readonly
end note

:Apply Policy Engine;

if (Secrets detected?) then (yes)
  :Block unsafe actions;
  :Allow only explain/summarize;
  -> blocked
else (no)
endif

if (Production or destructive?) then (yes)
  :Require human boundary;
  :Allow read-only / diagnostic capabilities;
else (no)
  :Allow profile capabilities;
endif

:Return classification result;

|AI Coder Agent|

:Call stable MCP tool:
actlane_load_capability;

|Actlane MCP Broker|

:Load selected capability contract;

note right
Capability contract contains:
- allowed operations
- forbidden operations
- required evidence
- max output budget
- human boundary
end note

:Return compact capability contract;

|AI Coder Agent|

:Call stable MCP tool:
actlane_run_capability;

|Actlane MCP Broker|

:Validate requested operation
against policy + capability contract;

if (Operation allowed?) then (yes)
  :Execute via adapter;
else (no)
  :Reject with reason;
  :Suggest safe next step;
  stop
endif

|Tool Adapter Layer|

:Run real tool or command;

note right
Examples:
- terraform fmt/validate/plan
- npm test/build/audit
- pytest/ruff/mypy
- github/gitlab CI query
- k8s readonly inspect
end note

|Actlane MCP Broker|

:Capture raw output;
:Store full output in Evidence Store;
:Compress context output;

note right
Raw logs do not go back
to the agent by default.

Agent receives:
- summary
- risk
- evidence_id
- next allowed actions
end note

:Return evidence summary;

|AI Coder Agent|

:Use summary to continue work;

if (Files / commands / facts changed?) then (yes)
  :Call actlane_classify again;
  note right
Runtime reclassification protects
against intent drift.
  end note
  |Actlane MCP Broker|
  :Recompute work type, risk flags, permissions;
  |AI Coder Agent|
else (no)
endif

:Call actlane_prepare_delivery
or actlane_explain;

|Actlane MCP Broker|

:Generate final safety summary;
:Attach evidence ids;
:Explain residual risk;
:State human boundary if needed;

|AI Coder Agent|

:Show user:
- what changed
- what was checked
- what is risky
- what needs human approval;

stop
@enduml